1. 🔍 WHAT IS DDL?
Real-World Analogy First

Imagine you're constructing a new apartment building.

Before anyone can live there, you must:

Buy land
Draw the blueprint
Build rooms
Add or remove rooms if needed
Demolish the building if necessary

DDL is exactly that.

It is not about putting furniture inside the rooms (data).

It is about creating and modifying the building itself (database structure).

Technical Definition

DDL stands for Data Definition Language.

It consists of SQL commands used to define and modify the structure of a database.

These commands work on the schema, not on the actual data.

🧠 Important Difference

Think of our bookstore.

